<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Kia Group shrs up on news of loan request.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Kia Group shrs up on news of loan request.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Kia Group rose slightly in early morning trading on Monday as investors believed two Kia affiliates would receive loans from state-run Korea Development Bank, brokers said.</p>
<p>An official at the bank said Kia Motors and Kia Steel had each asked the Korea Development Bank to extend 30 billion won each in loans.  </p>
<p>Kia Motors rose 100 won to 13,100 and Kia Steel gained 70 won to 3,370 at 0100 GMT.</p>
<p>The bank official said the state-run bank was now reviewing the request by the two Kia affiliates.</p>
<p>&quot;Investors believe the government will not stand idle in the face of Kia's financial problems, if there are any,&quot; said a Tongyang Securities broker.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
